  "id": "long-night-in-egypt",
  "title": "Long Night in Egypt",
  "subtitle": "A pyramid. A locked door. The Egyptian underworld is real and they are already inside it.",
  "description": "Long Night in Egypt is a supernatural horror podcast and limited audio drama series — eight episodes following a group of college students who enter the Pyramid of Unas on an unauthorized dig and find themselves trapped inside the Egyptian underworld. They went in looking for history. They found something that has been waiting for thousands of years. The door is locked behind them. The tunnels go deeper than the maps say they should. And the gods of ancient Egypt — Osiris, Anubis, the Ennead — are not mythology. They are present. They are watching. And every soul that enters the Duat must be judged. Eight episodes of Egyptian mythology horror. All available now. Written by Sarah Pitard. Directed by Jack Bowman. Score by Talip Peshkepia. Sound design by Jan Piasecki. Executive produced by Cassie Jozefov. A Violet Hour Media production. LISTENER WARNING: This program includes depictions of death and subject matter that may be upsetting for some listeners. Popular Topics Include: Egyptian mythology horror podcast, Egyptian underworld horror, pyramid horror podcast, Duat podcast, Anubis podcast, ancient Egypt horror fiction, mythology horror audio drama, supernatural horror podcast, horror fiction podcast, audio drama, scripted horror podcast, Egyptian mythology fiction, Pyramid of Unas, Ma'at, the Ennead, college students trapped horror, claustrophobic horror podcast, horror podcast like The Magnus Archives, horror podcast like Archive 81, horror podcast like Old Gods of Appalachia, horror podcast like The White Vault, Violet Hour Media.",
